  "extras": [
   {
    "title": "Residual Observations",
    "body": "Not open threats — no register entry is unmitigated. Recorded so they are not rediscovered\nas novel later.\n\n**`AUTH_MODE=dev` guard scope (relates to T-01-07).** `assert_safe_startup`\n(`backend/src/auth/mod.rs:197`) refuses to boot dev-bypass auth only when `BIND_ADDR` is\nnon-loopback. This host binds `127.0.0.1:8787` and is publicly exposed through cloudflared,\nwhich reaches the origin over loopback — so `AUTH_MODE=dev` in `portal.env` would boot\nwithout complaint and satisfy every session-gated route by injected identity while the\ntunnel kept serving the internet. T-01-07's mitigation is present exactly as planned; the\nobservation is that \"loopback bind\" stopped being a proxy for \"unreachable from outside\"\nonce the tunnel landed in 01-06. Production is verifiably unaffected: unauthenticated\n`GET /api/whoami` returns 401, which it would not under the dev bypass. Raised during the\nUAT test-3 route-inventory review and consciously accepted by the operator rather than\nlogged as a gap. Worth revisiting in Phase 2 — gate the bypass on a build feature, or have\nthe guard also refuse when a tunnel is configured.\n\n**`Cf-Connecting-Ip` tunnel dependency (relates to T-01-24).** OPEN-02 is resolved — the\nheader demonstrably survives the production tunnel (limiter-as-oracle, 2026-08-05). The\nresidual: the extractor falls back to `ConnectInfo<SocketAddr>` when the header is absent,\nwhich behind a tunnel is always `127.0.0.1`. A future loss of the header would collapse all\ncallers into one shared bucket silently rather than erroring. Recorded in `ops/README.md`\n§ Connecting-IP finding.\n\n**Unobserved fault windows (no threat ref).** Three UAT items were deferred rather than\nfailed and are catalogued in `01-UAT.md` § Notes: the AUTH-06 power-cut sub-case, the proxy\ngate's fail-closed path under a *valid* session cookie, and the authenticated header's\ndegradation when `/api/whoami` stops answering. The last two would close together in a\nsingle stopped-backend window. None contradicts a mitigation in this register; each is an\nobservation nobody has made."
   }
  ]
